PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Benin and Madagascar}

Explanation: The flag of Denmark, viewed as a color-pattern matrix with values chosen to maximize rank, has linear algebraic rank 2. Among African national flags, the ones whose maximal rank is also 2 are:

- **Benin**: green vertical stripe on the hoist, with yellow (top) and red (bottom) on the fly. Its essential matrix is  
  \[
  \begin{pmatrix}
  \text{green} & \text{yellow}\\
  \text{green} & \text{red}
  \end{pmatrix}
  \]
  which has rank 2 for distinct color values.

- **Madagascar**: white vertical stripe on the hoist, with red (top) and green (bottom) on the fly. Its essential matrix is  
  \[
  \begin{pmatrix}
  \text{white} & \text{red}\\
  \text{white} & \text{green}
  \end{pmatrix}
  \]
  which also has rank 2.

Other African flags either have rank 1 (simple horizontal/vertical tricolors) or rank 3 or higher due to additional independent features such as diagonal stripes, triangles, stars, crescents, or emblems. Thus the only African national flags with the same maximal linear algebraic rank as Denmark are **Benin and Madagascar**.

